      "writtenOn": "2026-09-30T05:51:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point: ALLOW/DENY precedence itself is not specific to aiReview.\n\nThe reason this test exists in the series is that the previous change moves aiReview from a custom default-allow path to Gerrit\u0027s standard ACL evaluation. So this test is intended as a regression check that aiReview now behaves like an ordinary change-scoped permission, including DENY canceling an ALLOW for the same tuple.\n\nIt is not meant to test the experiment flag. The experiment-specific coverage is the later no-grant / block-ignored cases. I can clarify the test name/comment, or trim the generic ACL matrix if you think the parent change already covers enough.",
