      "writtenOn": "2026-09-30T05:51:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree this is confusing, and I think the confusion comes from the temporary state of the series.\n\nToday aiReview has two separate pieces of technical debt:\n\n1. Permission semantics: it uses a custom default-allow path instead of Gerrit\u0027s normal default-deny ACL evaluation.\n2. UI transport: ActionJson smuggles a synthetic aiReview action because there is no server-side UiAction handler for it.\n\nI split the series so the first part fixes only (1): aiReview starts using normal ACL evaluation, while the existing ActionJson transport is kept temporarily so the UI keeps working at every commit.\n\nThat means the tests in this change still assert the old transport shape: when aiReview is denied, ActionJson emits a synthetic action with enabled\u003dfalse; when aiReview is allowed, the action is absent.\n\nThe second part fixes (2). Follow-up change 635823 removes this ActionJson smuggling after `GET /changes/{id}/permissions` exists, and moves the coverage to GetChangePermissionsIT where \"allowed\" is represented directly as the presence of \"aiReview\" in the permissions list.\n\nSo I can either keep this order and improve the comments/test names here, or move the `GET /permissions` endpoint earlier in the series to avoid this temporary ActionJson shape. I originally introduced `GET /permissions` earlier in the series, but changed the order later to make the semantic change reviewable in isolation.\n\nThe current split/order would also let us merge the first two semantic changes earlier:\n\n* Switch aiReview to default-deny semantics\n* Allow AI Review for registered users behind an experiment flag\n\nThose can be reviewed independently from the later UI transport cleanup.",
      "parentUuid": "848575c5_37d26f7d",
      "revId": "2ab9d72b6008a9e13ff23195c7885dd44297d31b",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
